# mm.build

The shared project and build model: the manifest walk, the dependency graph, the compiler and linker driver, shell quoting, and common process status handling. Application and target-runner command construction lives in mm.run.

The exported API lives in six partitions, listed before the primary interface
because source order is declared: :config holds the toolchain and lane
record; :manifest the tree model :config's SdkDefinition builds on;
:platform, :compile, :graph, and :external the analysis, driver, ordering,
and external-lane APIs that consume both. :detail holds the helpers more
than one implementation unit shares; it is not re-exported by the primary
interface, so importers of mm.build see exactly the six partitions. Each
implementation unit implements one partition's functions and imports the
partitions it consumes.
